  ── Shapiro-Wilk Test ───────────────────────
  Why: Formal test of whether the data are drawn from a normal distribution.
  W                   0.7465		Closer to 1 = more normal (range: 0 to 1)
  p                   < .001  (7.83e-09)		Statistically significant: if there were truly no effect, results at least this extreme would occur less than 0.1% of the time
  → Rejects normality (p < 0.05)


  ── Recommendation ──────────────────────────
  The evidence is against normality on the reading printed above.
  → Nonparametric tests (Mann-Whitney, Kruskal-Wallis, Spearman rho) are
     recommended.
  What was checked: the marginal distribution of this column. Parametric
  tests assume normality of the model RESIDUALS, which is not the same
  distribution and is not examined here.

  Conventions: quartiles R type 7 · SD & variance n-1
  · rank tests average tied ranks (tie-corrected).
